    {
      "id": "el84_448315526",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 976,
      "y": 1114.5,
      "width": 544.3,
      "height": 210,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "g_m2"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 946239001,
      "version": 2,
      "versionNonce": 1420017132,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789092764258,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "MV3        every Graph map is in memory — a worker restart loses every tab's stack,\n           so getActiveNodeId() throws and the popup renders nothing\n\ntraverse   the navigate event is suppressed for cross-origin destinations, so the\n           background must not depend on NAVIGATION_TRAVERSE arriving\n\ninternal   internalNodeId ≠ null ⇒ targetNode() already moved the cursor; the router\n           only verifies where it landed, never steps again (one event per go())\n\nrevisit    Chrome drops old entries — those nodes are re-navigated instead of\n           traversed to, and the new node is linked back through revisitOf\n\nstale      content scripts from a previous build keep sending old strings until the\n           tab is reloaded — parseMessage is what catches them",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "MV3        every Graph map is in memory — a worker restart loses every tab's stack,\n           so getActiveNodeId() throws and the popup renders nothing\n\ntraverse   the navigate event is suppressed for cross-origin destinations, so the\n           background must not depend on NAVIGATION_TRAVERSE arriving\n\ninternal   internalNodeId ≠ null ⇒ targetNode() already moved the cursor; the router\n           only verifies where it landed, never steps again (one event per go())\n\nrevisit    Chrome drops old entries — those nodes are re-navigated instead of\n           traversed to, and the new node is linked back through revisitOf\n\nstale      content scripts from a previous build keep sending old strings until the\n           tab is reloaded — parseMessage is what catches them",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "index": "b0M"
    }
  ],
